WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.030 --> 00:00:08.689
"What?" Ally gulped. "Did you say we have to fight off extraterrestrials, Dr. Lloyd?"

2
00:00:08.691 --> 00:00:11.100
The alien life expert shrugged.

3
00:00:11.101 --> 00:00:14.816
"Well, there's a small chance they've come to Earth in peace.

4
00:00:14.817 --> 00:00:18.432
But either way, I need to share everything that I've learned.

5
00:00:18.433 --> 00:00:22.057
That's why I'm having a special exhibit at the convention."

6
00:00:22.058 --> 00:00:28.630
"Sounds great," Ally said with a smile. "Well, I've got to get going now."

7
00:00:28.631 --> 00:00:32.131
"Oh, but you can't leave!" Dr. Lloyd said.

8
00:00:32.132 --> 00:00:37.934
"I want to give you a sneak preview of my exhibit. And I won't take no for an answer."

9
00:00:37.935 --> 00:00:41.206
"You sure?" Ally asked nervously.

10
00:00:41.207 --> 00:00:51.818
Dr. Lloyd laughed. "You are a funny one, Ally! Come along, the exhibit is this way."

11
00:00:51.819 --> 00:00:55.336
He led Ally to a small gallery at the end of the main exhibit hall.

12
00:00:55.337 --> 00:01:00.350
As Ally passed through the doorway, a loud alarm sounded, sending Ally jumping.

13
00:01:00.351 --> 00:01:08.778
Dr. Lloyd groaned. "I forgot all about the new metal detector that Security installed.

14
00:01:08.779 --> 00:01:12.783
Just empty your pockets of anything metal and put it on the tray."

15
00:01:12.784 --> 00:01:18.434
"Okay." Ally took off her bracelet and hair clip and started through the doorway again.

16
00:01:18.435 --> 00:01:20.213
Brrp! Brrp!

17
00:01:20.214 --> 00:01:26.174
"Hmm." Dr. Lloyd frowned. "Perhaps you've forgotten to remove a piece of jewelry?"

18
00:01:26.175 --> 00:01:28.531
Ally shook her head.

19
00:01:28.532 --> 00:01:35.235
"No?" Dr. Lloyd pointed to her neck. "I see a necklace chain.

20
00:01:35.236 --> 00:01:37.780
Slip that off, and you can breeze right through."

21
00:01:37.781 --> 00:01:41.532
Ally's hand flew up to where her meld medallion was hidden beneath her clothes.

22
00:01:41.533 --> 00:01:44.131
"I can't take this off!"

23
00:01:44.132 --> 00:01:45.685
"Why not?"

24
00:01:45.686 --> 00:01:48.608
"What do I do?" Ally thought frantically.

25
00:01:48.609 --> 00:01:53.024
"If I take it off, I'll revert to my Astralian form!"

26
00:01:53.025 --> 00:01:59.107
"Um, because when my parents gave it to me, they warned me never to take it off.

27
00:01:59.108 --> 00:02:04.259
It would be . . . bad luck! I'll just leave and come back another time."

28
00:02:04.260 --> 00:02:07.174
Ally turned to go, but Dr. Lloyd stopped her.

29
00:02:07.175 --> 00:02:11.461
"Don't be silly. I'll just ask the guards to turn the alarm off.

30
00:02:11.462 --> 00:02:15.015
They've been having lots of problems with these metal detectors anyway.

31
00:02:15.016 --> 00:02:24.507
Come along. I can't wait to let you peek at my findings!"

32
00:02:24.508 --> 00:02:28.191
Ally trudged after Dr. Lloyd, trying to hide her frustration.

33
00:02:28.192 --> 00:02:33.869
So far, her shopping trip for parts was a total failure.

34
00:02:33.870 --> 00:02:39.076
*** Inside the gallery the walls were covered in large drawings of extraterrestrial beings.

35
00:02:39.077 --> 00:02:41.931
Dr. Lloyd stopped in front of one of them.

36
00:02:41.932 --> 00:02:48.263
To Ally, the creature in the sketch looked strange, like a combination of a GreyZoner and a Gorphelian.

37
00:02:48.264 --> 00:02:51.028
But Dr. Lloyd was pointing proudly to the sketch.

38
00:02:51.029 --> 00:02:58.559
"According to my research, the life-forms on Gamma89B are much more technologically advanced than we Earthlings are."

39
00:02:58.560 --> 00:03:04.026
"Huh?" Ally thought. She'd never heard of a planet called Gamma89B.

40
00:03:04.027 --> 00:03:08.185
Next he showed her a model of a weapon called a delta hydroblaster.

41
00:03:08.186 --> 00:03:11.282
"This is a very popular weapon among aliens.

42
00:03:11.283 --> 00:03:15.605
It has the power to disintegrate a cement wall in an instant.

43
00:03:15.606 --> 00:03:19.495
If they attack us with these, we'll be utterly defenseless."

44
00:03:19.496 --> 00:03:22.011
Ally forced a smile to hide her surprise.

45
00:03:22.012 --> 00:03:26.193
"There's no such thing as a delta hydroblaster," she thought.

46
00:03:26.194 --> 00:03:30.193
"What in the world is he talking about?"

47
00:03:30.194 --> 00:03:35.578
Then Dr. Lloyd showed her a map of the outer reaches of the universe.

48
00:03:35.579 --> 00:03:39.511
"Everything is mislabeled!" Ally thought in horror.

49
00:03:39.512 --> 00:03:43.907
"I can't let Dr. Lloyd go on believing all this crazy stuff.

50
00:03:43.908 --> 00:03:48.602
Astralians are supposed to enlighten the universe!"

51
00:03:48.603 --> 00:03:51.930
"You know, Dr. Lloyd," she said carefully.

52
00:03:51.931 --> 00:03:57.715
"My mother is an astronomer, so she's taught me a lot about space."

53
00:03:57.716 --> 00:03:59.942
This wasn't really a lie.

54
00:03:59.943 --> 00:04:07.179
Ally's mother, like every other adult on Astralia, had completed advanced studies in astronomy.

55
00:04:07.180 --> 00:04:12.795
"Fascinating!" Dr. Lloyd said. "So what do you think of all my discoveries?"

56
00:04:12.796 --> 00:04:19.403
"First of all, I doubt extraterrestrials want to hurt humans," Ally said.

57
00:04:19.404 --> 00:04:24.027
"If you think about it, space is a very quiet place.

58
00:04:24.028 --> 00:04:27.458
Why would anyone want to disturb the peace?"

59
00:04:27.459 --> 00:04:34.135
She held her breath. Her argument didn't really make a lot of sense, but Dr. Lloyd cocked his head, looking intrigued.

60
00:04:34.136 --> 00:04:37.408
"Interesting theory!" he said.

61
00:04:37.409 --> 00:04:43.170
"Now I really insist—you must come to Friday's opening as my special guest.

62
00:04:43.171 --> 00:04:46.063
My colleagues are other leading experts in the field.

63
00:04:46.064 --> 00:04:50.433
You'll have the opportunity to discuss lots of your ideas."

64
00:04:50.434 --> 00:04:54.605
"Awesome!" Ally said quickly. "Thanks—see you at the opening!"

65
00:04:54.606 --> 00:04:58.112
As she hurried off, her mind was racing.

66
00:04:58.113 --> 00:05:02.097
"I absolutely have to be gone by Friday now," she thought.

67
00:05:02.098 --> 00:05:09.898
"Being in a room full of experts on alien life sounds dangerous—really, really dangerous!"

